# Prettier is scoped to the mod's XML and nothing else. Everything in this repo is either
# hand-formatted, owned by another tool (Python by ruff, shell by shfmt), or a preserved
# provenance document — so the safe default is to ignore all of it and opt mod/ back in.
#
# NOTE the directory re-includes below. Gitignore semantics cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is still excluded, so `*` followed by only `!mod/**/*.xml` silently matches
# nothing at all — and `prettier --check` then passes by inspecting zero files.
*
!mod/
!mod/**/
!mod/**/*.xml
!mod/**/*.rpm

# Mura's original documents are a provenance record and are never reformatted.
docs/2.2-changelog.txt
docs/mura-feature-notes-wip.txt
